{
  "message_id": "benefits-designer-02",
  "speech": "Director, I support your nine-unit scope and your current no-release decision. Access's actual advice changes my preference: I accept funding the assisted slot and dropping my separate wording change. Human review 2, assistance 2, tracking 2, participatory check 2 and consultation 1 total nine. We must retain the confusion reported in B-H1 as an unresolved limitation, without quietly adding unfunded wording work.\n\nOn your policy question, B-P1 establishes only that ambiguous claims require authorized human review and that page completion has no eligibility meaning. It does not supply substantive approval criteria or general closure criteria; I cannot fill those gaps. Under B-P2, I can approve a routing specification against that narrow rule.\n\nMy proposed acceptance test is to trace an ambiguous claim through the specified workflow: completing its pages must confer no eligibility approval, must not itself trigger closure, and must leave an identifiable referral awaiting authorized human review. We should inspect the routing record and completion-trigger behavior. Actual availability of an authorized recipient remains unestablished, so passing a specification check would not establish an operational review route or justify release.\n\nI accept access's recommendation for an observed walkthrough and its explicit limitations: recruitment, tested coverage and access readiness remain unresolved; consultation is not validation. Those are attributed recommendations, not my specialist signoff.\n\nCan you obtain evidence of a named authorized reviewer, available review capacity and a workable handoff within the fortnight? Until then, I support documenting the bounded plan with no release. My policy signoff covers the stated routing constraint only, not eligibility decisions or access readiness.",
  "evidence_disclosed": ["B-H1", "B-P1", "B-P2"],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Support the nine-unit allocation of human review 2, assistance 2, tracking 2, participatory check 2 and consultation 1, excluding a separate wording change and retaining interview-reported confusion as unresolved.",
      "basis": ["benefits-director-02", "benefits-access-01", "public.cost_reference", "B-H1"],
      "competency": "plain-language workflow design",
      "standing": "role_judgment"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The supplied rule requires authorized human review for ambiguous claims and gives page completion no eligibility meaning; substantive approval criteria and general closure criteria are not supplied.",
      "basis": ["B-P1", "B-P2"],
      "competency": "specified fictional policy application",
      "standing": "role_judgment"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Approve only the routing constraint against the supplied rule, with a proposed test tracing an ambiguous claim to an identifiable referral awaiting authorized human review, checking that page completion confers no approval and does not itself trigger closure.",
      "basis": ["B-P1", "B-P2", "benefits-director-02"],
      "competency": "specified fictional policy application",
      "standing": "role_judgment"
    },
    {
      "claim": "A specification check does not establish operational authorized-review availability; support no release while that availability remains unestablished, without extending policy signoff to eligibility decisions or access readiness.",
      "basis": ["B-P1", "B-P2", "benefits-director-02", "benefits-access-01"],
      "competency": "specified fictional policy application",
      "standing": "role_judgment"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Accept the consultant's recommendation for an observed walkthrough while retaining the consultant's unresolved recruitment, tested-coverage and access-readiness limitations; this is attributed advice, not independent specialist validation.",
      "basis": ["benefits-access-01"],
      "competency": "plain-language workflow design",
      "standing": "attributed_advice"
    }
  ],
  "consult_request": null,
  "decision": "commitment"
}

